FINDING: CY is applied as a pure body-y force, NOT rotated through beta. The docstring says so explicitly ('Side force is already body-axis, as the lateral derivatives are defined'), and CR-2144's CY_beta is indeed a body-axis derivative, so this is a stated convention rather than a defect. Consequence: the side force is not perpendicular to the relative wind at beta != 0, so it does a small amount of work along the flight path -- second order in beta (cos(F,v) ~ sin(beta)).
